              "text": "The latest version of Python can be downloaded directly from the official **Python Software Foundation** website:\n\n*   **Official Downloads Page:** **[python.org/downloads](https://www.python.org/downloads/)**\n\n### Current Version Information\nThe latest stable version is **Python 3.14.x** (specifically **3.14.5**). \n\n### How to Install Based on Your Operating System:\n\n*   **Windows:** \n    *   Go to the downloads page and click the yellow **\"Download Python 3.14.x\"** button.\n    *   **Important Step:** When running the installer, make sure to check the box at the bottom that says **\"Add Python to PATH\"** (or \"Add python.exe to PATH\") before clicking \"Install Now\". This ensures you can run Python from your Command Prompt or PowerShell.\n    *   Alternatively, you can get the official [Python Install Manager from the Microsoft Store](https://apps.microsoft.com/detail/9p0t03zg8v26).\n\n*   **macOS:**\n    *   The website will automatically detect your OS and provide a macOS `.pkg` installer. Download and run it.\n    *   Alternatively, if you use the [Homebrew](https://brew.sh/) package manager, you can install it via your Terminal by running: \n        ```bash\n        brew install python\n        ```\n\n*   **Linux / UNIX:**\n    *   Most Linux distributions come with Python pre-installed. \n    *   If you need to update to the latest version, it is highly recommended to use your distribution's package manager (e.g., `sudo apt update && sudo apt install python3` on Ubuntu/Debian) rather than compiling from the source, to avoid breaking system dependencies.",
